{% comment %}
  The day - every meeting drawn where it falls.

  A list tells you what is on. This tells you what the day is *shaped* like:
  where the wall of back-to-back things is, where the two free hours are, and
  which two meetings somebody booked on top of each other. It is the one view
  that answers "can I take this call at four" without arithmetic.

  Three things it has to get right, all of which the list views get away with
  ignoring:

    - The window has to hold everything. It starts as the hours the widget was
      given and stretches to cover any meeting outside them, so an eight
      o'clock start never hides a seven o'clock flight.
    - Two things at once go side by side. Which column each takes is worked out
      in lib/calendar/day.ts, because it is a graph colouring and a template is
      a bad place to find that out.
    - A block too short to hold its own title has to say something anyway. A
      fifteen-minute standup is four per cent of a day, and four per cent of
      480 pixels is nineteen - enough for a rule and a time, not for words.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign day = calendar -%}
{%- assign hh = "now" | date: "%H" | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign now_mins = "now" | date: "%M" | plus: hh -%}

{%- comment %} How many are actually left, counted against the clock at the
  moment of drawing rather than taken from the payload. `today.remaining` was
  true when Google was last asked, which is up to ten minutes ago, and this
  design decides what to *say* from the live clock - so the two disagree for
  the whole of that window and the panel prints "6 left" beside "Nothing left
  today". Same reason the countdowns are worked out here. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign left = 0 -%}
{%- for event in day.events -%}
  {%- if event.end_minutes > now_mins %}{% assign left = left | plus: 1 %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign gone = day.today.total | minus: left | at_least: 0 -%}

{%- assign box_w = shape.width | at_least: 160 -%}
{%- assign box_h = shape.height | at_least: 240 -%}
{%- assign pad = box_w | divided_by: 24 | at_least: 8 | at_most: 18 -%}

{%- comment %} The stretch of day to draw: what was asked for, widened to hold
  anything outside it, and always containing the time it is now. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign open = extension.values.day_start | default: "08:00" | minutes_of -%}
{%- assign close = extension.values.day_end | default: "20:00" | minutes_of -%}

{%- for event in day.events -%}
  {%- if event.start_minutes < open -%}
    {%- assign open = event.start_minutes | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if event.end_minutes > close -%}
    {%- assign close = event.end_minutes | plus: 59 | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if now_mins < open %}{% assign open = now_mins | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if now_mins > close %}{% assign close = now_mins | plus: 59 | divided_by: 60 | times: 60 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign span = close | minus: open | at_least: 120 -%}

{%- comment %} Whether the day is behind you. The ribbon still draws it - what
  is over is the point of a day view at six o'clock - but a track with a rule
  across the bottom of it and nothing else to say is the design at its most
  useless, so the space under it is spent on the next thing there is. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign spent = false -%}
{%- if left == 0 %}{% assign spent = true %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign header = 44 -%}
{%- if day.all_day.size > 0 and box_h > 260 %}{% assign header = header | plus: 26 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if notices.size > 0 %}{% assign header = header | plus: 34 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign footer = false -%}
{%- if spent and box_h > 210 %}{% assign footer = true %}{% assign header = header | plus: 40 %}{% endif -%}
{%- assign track_h = box_h | minus: header | minus: pad | minus: pad | at_least: 120 -%}

{%- comment %} How often the hours are labelled, so they never collide: a
  twelve-hour day in 300 pixels is 25 pixels an hour, which is one label every
  two. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign hours = span | divided_by: 60 -%}
{%- assign per_hour = track_h | divided_by: hours | at_least: 1 -%}
{%- assign every = 1 -%}
{%- if per_hour < 30 %}{% assign every = 2 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if per_hour < 15 %}{% assign every = 3 %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign gutter = 34 -%}
{%- if box_w < 220 %}{% assign gutter = 28 %}{% endif -%}

<div class="screen{% if box_w < 260 %} dense{% endif %}">
  <div class="title-bar" style="padding: {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px 7px">
    <div class="title" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 18 | at_least: 15 | at_most: 28 }}px">
      {{ extension.values.heading | default: day.today.day }}
    </div>
    <div class="t-xs t-bold">{{ day.today.busy_text }} booked</div>
  </div>

  {% if day.all_day.size > 0 and box_h > 260 %}
    <div style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 4px {{ pad }}px">
      <p class="t-xs t-bold truncate">
        {% for entry in day.all_day %}{{ entry.title }}{% unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
      </p>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  <div class="content" style="padding: {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px 0">
    <div style="position: relative; height: 100%; width: 100%">
      {%- comment %} The hours, as rules across the track with their labels in
        the gutter beside it. The track is its own box inset by the gutter, so
        that every percentage below is a percentage of the *track* - work them
        out against the whole width instead and a meeting in the second column
        hangs off the right-hand edge by exactly one gutter. {% endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%} Floored: a day that starts at 07:30 is still hour seven. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign first_hour = open | divided_by: 60 | floor -%}
      {%- assign last_hour = close | divided_by: 60 | floor -%}
      {% for hour in (first_hour..last_hour) %}
        {%- assign at = hour | times: 60 | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
        {%- assign since = hour | minus: first_hour -%}
        {%- assign nth = since | modulo: every -%}
        {% if at >= 0 and at <= 1000 and nth == 0 %}
          <span class="t-xs" style="position: absolute; top: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0;
                      width: {{ gutter | minus: 6 }}px; text-align: right;
                      transform: translateY(-50%); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums">{{ hour }}</span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      <div style="position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: {{ gutter }}px; right: 0">
      {% for hour in (first_hour..last_hour) %}
        {%- assign at = hour | times: 60 | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
        {% if at >= 0 and at <= 1000 %}
          <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0; right: 0;
                      border-top: 1px solid var(--ink)"></div>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}

      {%- comment %} Where the day has got to, drawn *under* the meetings. A
        rule across the whole track says where you are at a glance; laid over
        the top it also puts a black bar through the title of whatever you are
        sitting in. {% endcomment -%}
      {%- assign now_at = now_mins | minus: open | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
      {% if now_at >= 0 and now_at <= 1000 %}
        <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ now_at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: 0; right: 0; height: 3px;
                    background: var(--ink)"></div>
      {% endif %}

      {%- comment %} The meetings. Overlapping ones share the width by the
        lanes worked out at fetch, so a double booking reads as two blocks side
        by side rather than as one block hiding another. {% endcomment -%}
      {% for event in day.events %}
        {%- assign from = event.start_minutes | minus: open -%}
        {%- assign until = event.end_minutes | minus: open -%}
        {%- if until > 0 and from < span -%}
          {%- if from < 0 %}{% assign from = 0 %}{% endif -%}
          {%- if until > span %}{% assign until = span %}{% endif -%}
          {%- assign top = from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
          {%- assign tall = until | minus: from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
          {%- assign block_px = until | minus: from | times: track_h | divided_by: span -%}
          {%- assign lane_w = 100 | divided_by: event.lanes -%}
          {%- assign lane_at = event.lane | times: lane_w -%}
          {%- assign done = false -%}
          {%- if event.end_minutes <= now_mins %}{% assign done = true %}{% endif -%}
          {%- assign running = false -%}
          {%- if done == false and event.start_minutes <= now_mins %}{% assign running = true %}{% endif -%}

          {%- comment %} What is over is drawn anyway, hatched. A day view that
            empties as it goes loses the thing it is for - at four o'clock you
            want to see that the morning was solid, not a blank half a
            ribbon. {% endcomment -%}
          <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ top | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; height: {{ tall | divided_by: 10.0 }}%;
                      left: {{ lane_at }}%; width: calc({{ lane_w }}% - 3px);
                      min-height: 10px; overflow: hidden;
                      border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 1px 4px;
                      {% if running %}border-left-width: 7px; padding-left: 3px;{% endif %}
                      {% if done %}background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--paper) 0 4px, var(--ink) 4px 5px)
                      {% else %}background: var(--paper){% endif %}">
            {% if block_px >= 34 %}
              <span class="t-xs t-bold" style="display: block; line-height: 1.15">{{ event.start }}</span>
              <span class="t-xs truncate" style="display: block; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.2">{{ event.title }}</span>
              {% if block_px >= 64 and extension.values.show_location != false and event.location != blank %}
                <span class="t-xs truncate" style="display: block; font-weight: 400">{{ event.location }}</span>
              {% endif %}
            {% elsif block_px >= 16 %}
              {%- comment %} Too short for two lines: the time and as much of
                the title as the width carries, on one. Shorter than this and
                it carries none at all and is filled in instead - a quarter of
                an hour is six pixels of a twelve-hour day, and six pixels of
                clipped type reads as a broken screen rather than as a short
                meeting. {% endcomment -%}
              <span class="truncate" style="display: block; line-height: 1; font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700;
                           {% if done %}background: var(--paper){% endif %}">
                {{ event.start }} {{ event.title }}
              </span>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      {% endfor %}

      </div>

      {% if now_at >= 0 and now_at <= 1000 %}
        <div style="position: absolute; top: {{ now_at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; left: {{ gutter | minus: 8 }}px;
                    transform: translateY(-50%); width: 0; height: 0;
                    border-top: 5px solid transparent; border-bottom: 5px solid transparent;
                    border-left: 7px solid var(--ink)"></div>
      {% endif %}

      {%- comment %} Nothing was ever on this day, so the track is an empty
        grid - which reads as a widget that failed rather than as a free day.
        Said plainly, over the hours it is talking about. {% endcomment -%}
      {% if day.today.total == 0 %}
        <div style="position: absolute; top: 50%; left: {{ gutter | plus: 6 }}px; right: 6px;
                    transform: translateY(-50%); background: var(--paper);
                    border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 10px 8px; text-align: center">
          {%- comment %} About this day, not about the window: with Friday in
            the payload, "Nothing this week" over an empty Thursday is simply
            untrue. {% endcomment -%}
          <p class="t-xs t-bold">{% if day.next_any %}Nothing today{% else %}{{ day.empty_label | default: "Nothing today" }}{% endif %}</p>
          {% if day.all_day.size > 0 %}
            <p class="t-xs truncate" style="margin-top: 3px">
              {% for entry in day.all_day %}{{ entry.title }}{% unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless %}{% endfor %}
            </p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>

  {% if footer %}
    <div class="footer-bar" style="padding: 7px {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px; font-size: 13px">
      {% if day.next_any and day.next_any.start_minutes > now_mins %}
        <span class="t-bold truncate">
          {{ day.next_any_day }} {{ day.next_any.start }} &middot; {{ day.next_any.title }}
        </span>
        {% if box_w > 260 %}<span class="t-xs" style="flex: none; white-space: nowrap">next</span>{% endif %}
      {% else %}
        <span class="t-bold truncate">{{ day.empty_label | default: "Nothing left today" }}</span>

        <span class="t-xs" style="flex: none; white-space: nowrap">
          {% if gone > 0 %}{{ gone }} done, {{ day.today.busy_text }}{% endif %}
        </span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {% if notices.size > 0 %}
    <div class="notice-strip" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px">
      {% for notice in notices %}
        {% if notice.overflow %}
          <span class="notice notice--more">+{{ notice.overflow }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="notice notice--{{ notice.level }}" title="{{ notice.text }}">
            <span class="i i-{{ notice.icon }}"></span>
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if shape.wide and notices[0].text != blank %}
        <span class="notice-said">{{ notices[0].text }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
